a setting of the EXPLAIN query does not change what CREATE accepted
status:       applicable
a new column that the index does not read keeps the index
status:       applicable
a type change of a column that the index reads makes the index not applicable
status:       not_applicable
reason:       Hypothetical index no longer matches the table: column `b` was UInt64, now UInt32. Run CREATE HYPOTHETICAL INDEX again
a new column under SELECT * makes the projection not applicable
status:       not_applicable
reason:       Hypothetical projection no longer matches the table: the columns under `*` were (a, b, c), now (a, b, c, d). Run CREATE HYPOTHETICAL PROJECTION again
